  "query_preview": "../ Sunday to Wednesday /  Sunday is looking like it \nmay be the break day for weather for SEAK, as incoming low/short \nwave will undercut the panhandle moving over the Haida Gwaii and \nBritish Columbia coastal area as it landfalls Sunday. Southern \nportion of the panhandle may get some rain out of the associated \nrain shield. THe northern panhandle and Northeast gulf coast \nregion would be a drier off short pattern briefly. Also not a big \ngradient so winds should be a bit more relaxed. \n\nThe model solutions for Monday have an agreement that a low will \nmove from the Pacific into the eastern-central gulf  with a roughly \na 960-965 low into the gulf Monday morning. the track of this one \nlooks similar to the Thursday system. Will expect quite strong winds \nfor marine zones  probably up to Storm force.  The Southwest islands \nof the panhandle  may end up with public hazards as well for Monday. \nStay tuned for updates to the situation.",
